# cppcheck suppressions for the `cppcheck` CMake target / CI job.
#
# Each entry below is a reviewed false positive or an explicitly scoped-out
# category, not a blanket "make the tool quiet" - see the comment above each
# group for the reasoning. Add a comment before any new line here.

# Vendored code under third_party/ (and system/SDK headers pulled in via -I,
# e.g. freetype2) is not ours to fix.
*:*/third_party/*
*:/usr/include/*

# This is a long-standing C++03/11-style codebase where many small
# value/handle types deliberately leave POD members (ints, pointers, enums)
# uninitialized at declaration and set them from the constructor body, an
# obvious initializer that immediately follows construction, or (for
# BitPixelAccess::operator=, see doc/image_iterator.h) a proxy type that
# intentionally does not copy its own members on assignment. Spot-checked
# several (doc/image_iterator.h, render.cpp, flic/decoder.cpp) - all
# confirmed intentional. Revisit if a *specific* one is suspected of a real
# bug rather than re-enabling this wholesale.
uninitMemberVar
uninitMemberVarNoCtor
uninitMemberVarPrivate
operatorEqVarError

# C-style casts throughout doc/ and app/file/*_format.cpp are between
# related numeric/pointer types in pixel-format conversion and file-decoding
# hot paths. Rewriting ~25 of them to static_cast/reinterpret_cast one by
# one without per-cast type verification and a full image-correctness
# re-test risks silently changing behavior; left as a follow-up
# modernization task rather than a mechanical find-and-replace.
dangerousTypeCast
intToPointerCast

# Long-standing style in this codebase: RAII-owning types are generally not
# made non-copyable by declaring a copy-ctor/operator= pair, they're just
# never copied. Not a correctness issue on its own.
noCopyConstructor
noOperatorEq

# Style opinions with no correctness impact.
returnByReference
useInitializationList
duplInheritedMember
passedByValue
stlIfStrFind
stlcstrParam
